===21st Century===
In recent years, the relationship between the countries has been significantly narrowed through visits by senior officials, multilateral dialogue, increased trade and cooperation, especially in aerospace and technical-military matters. Balisca and the Soviet Union have established themselves as "Strategic Partners and Technological Allies". The two countries maintain regular political dialogue on security, counter-terrorism and global issues, and have since 2021, shared intelligence. This dialogue has now been incorporated into the {{W|International security|Global Security Talks}}, which allow high-level officials to share concerns and solutions on non-proliferation, regional issues and defense relations. In 2006, the two countries jointly launched [[Project Luna Horizons]].

Balisca and the Soviet Union have converging positions on many issues on the international agenda, sharing the conviction that it is necessary to reform the structures of global governance, with a view to building an institutional architecture more consistent with the contemporary world. In 1995, Soviet officials invited the [[Confederal Armed Forces]] to participate in the annual {{W|Moscow Victory Day Parade}}, in which the Baliscan military dispatched a {{W|Company (military unit)|company}} of 100 airmen to participate. Additionally, the two countries have increasingly found themselves aligned with one another on the international stage: Balisca and Soviet intelligence agencies cooperated extensively during the [[South Atlantic War]]. The Soviet Union supported Baliscan efforts to diplomatically free the [[Baliscan duo]] during their detention by authorities in the [[West Pacific]]. At the {{W|United Nations}}, the Soviet Union has supported Balisca's aspirations to {{W|Reform of the UNSC|gain a}} {{W|permanent member of the UNSC|permanent seat on the UNSC}}, and the two countries coordinate diplomatic and economic moves, and the consolidation of a non-interventionist foreign policy.

